      "title": "Post Doc Res Assoc - Physics & Astronomy",
      "description": "Short Description for Internal Candidates\t\nThe Department of Physics & Astronomy at the University of Wyoming is seeking to fill a Postdoctoral Scholar position in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics. Candidates must hold a doctoral degree in physics, materials sciences, electrical engineering or a closely related area. The successful candidates will participate in the research program of Prof. Jifa Tian’s research lab to investigate the nontrivial quantum phenomena in 2D materials. The project involves 2D materials preparation and handling, quantum device fabrication, and transport measurements at low temperatures. Preference will be given to those with demonstrated ability to carry out effective and productive research, demonstrated ability for effective communication with faculty, staff, and students, and experience in at least one of the above-mentioned areas. Applications must include a cover letter, CV, and statement of research interests. ",
